{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And you shall rejoice in your festival.</b> Above, regarding Shavuot, it mentioned rejoicing, because it is the time of harvest and a time of joy, as it is written: 'they rejoice before you as with joy at harvest'; how much more so now regarding Sukkot, when everything has been gathered from the field. But regarding Pesach it did not mention rejoicing, because the essence of the festival is the remembrance of the miracle of the exodus from Egypt, and furthermore there is not yet primary joy in purchasing grain. And furthermore we learned in the fourth chapter: the world is judged on Pesach regarding the grain, and perhaps hail or locust, grasshopper, blasting, mildew, will strike them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:04.446771914Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}